From 8173cc6b9011ffdaf3c788e280644c6447aa2bd3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dwc2d <dwc2d@localhost>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 06:05:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dwc2d: poll the keyboard on the channel interrupt instead
 of spinning

Each poll of a low-speed keyboard behind a hub waited for its start and
complete split, about 130 us of spinning 50 times a second on the Pi
(row 242, #211). The channel halt now raises the controller interrupt,
which sends the complete split or takes the report. A timer check stops
a poll after 50 ms in case an interrupt is lost.
